{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"ReviewDraftTool|deferred|not-used|tools|evidence\" pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go | head -90'","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:8:// the criteria and tools the plan owes, the structural facts and the sealed\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:9:// evidence. The brief renders exactly that, deterministically, with fixed\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:126:const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:130:// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:131:// evidence, and what a mapping's basis is.\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:141:\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:146:\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:355:\t\tline(\"Review the change below against the scope's requirements and the criteria the plan owes. Read the code and run the tests you need; judge each criterion with your own evidence.\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:357:\t\tline(\"Give an independent verdict on the questions the scope records (its decisions, outcomes and requirement trace), using only the sealed evidence and what you can reproduce. Say for each whether the record holds, and why.\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:418:\t\tevidence := \"\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:420:\t\t\tevidence = \"; evidence: \" + strings.Join(c.EvidenceClasses, \", \")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:422:\t\tline(\"- %s (%s, %s%s): %s\", c.ID, ReviewCriterionKind(c), required, evidence, c.Description)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:433:\t\ttools := append([]ReviewPlanTool(nil), plan.Tools...)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:434:\t\tsort.SliceStable(tools, func(i, j int) bool { return tools[i].ID+tools[i].Component < tools[j].ID+tools[j].Component })\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:435:\t\tfor _, t := range tools {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:442:\t\t\t\tclasses = \"; evidence classes: \" + strings.Join(t.EvidenceClasses, \", \")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:481:\tline(\"## Sealed evidence\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:483:\tevidence := append([]ReviewBundleEvidence(nil), bundle.Payload.Evidence...)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:484:\tsort.Slice(evidence, func(i, j int) bool { return evidence[i].ID < evidence[j].ID })\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:485:\tfor _, e := range evidence {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:529:\t\t\tline(\"5. At the end, the verdict POSE records as each surface's smoke evidence: one fenced block opened with ```pose-draft holding a JSON object with `schema` %q, `decision` (the decision above), `findings` (each with `id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line` and `summary`) and `surfaces` (one entry per surface above, each with `ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands` you ran and what you `observed`). A surface you do not answer records no evidence. Everything outside the block is yours and is not read.\", ReviewDraftSchema)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:535:\t\tline(\"2. For each question above: whether the record holds, does not hold, or cannot be determined from the sealed evidence and what you can reproduce, and why.\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:537:\t\tline(\"4. At the end, the verdict POSE records for the scope: one fenced block opened with ```pose-draft holding a JSON object with `schema` %q, `decision` (the decision above), `findings` (each with `id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line` and `summary`) and `questions` (one entry per question above, each with `id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence` and `rationale`). A question you do not answer is not answered for you. Everything outside the block is yours and is not read.\", ReviewDraftSchema)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:541:\tline(\"2. For each criterion above: passed, failed or not-applicable, with your evidence (a sealed evidence ref, a command you ran, or file and line).\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:554:\t\t\tline(\"%d. In the same block, the conclusion POSE records as the attestation: `criteria` (one entry per criterion above, each with `id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>` — a class the criterion asks for when it names one — and `rationale` for not-applicable), and `tools` (one entry per tool above, each with `id`, `component` when it has one, `disposition`, `evidence` and `rationale`). A follow-up finding that should be accepted as a risk carries `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; any other finding stays open. A criterion or tool you do not answer is not answered for you.\", next+1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:582:\t\treturn \", `prior_findings` (each with `id`, `status` and `evidence`, one for every finding of the previous round; the `id` is the identifier listed under Findings to account for, which carries its round, for example R2-F1, never a bare F1, and a finding you report now takes an `id` that no earlier round used, for example N1: a bare or reused identifier makes the whole draft unreadable) and `sweep` (what you swept)\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:584:\treturn \", `prior_findings` (each with `id`, `status` and `evidence`, one for every finding of the previous round) and `sweep` (what you swept)\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
