red\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:50:\t\"lacks a required evidence class\":                                                                   \"when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:70:\t\"review-complete\":                       \"a precondition name, not a message\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:71:\t\"delivery-target-declared\":              \"a precondition name, not a message\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:31:\t\t\"missing criterion\":                                          {\"every required criterion and every tool above is answered\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:32:\t\t\"review tool has invalid disposition\":                        {\"`passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:34:\t\t\"required review tool was not used\":                          {\"`not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:35:\t\t\"recommended review tool lacks not-used rationale\":           {\"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go:38:\t\t\"review tool lacks a required evidence class\":                {\"when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_domain_preflight_test.go:160:\t\t{\"missing tool\", func(_ preflightFixture, att *ReviewAttestation) { att.Tools = nil }, \"missing required review tool disposition\"},\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:126:const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:130:// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:141:\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:146:\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:554:\t\t\tline(\"%d. In the same block, the conclusion POSE records as the attestation: `criteria` (one entry per criterion above, each with `id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>` — a class the criterion asks for when it names one — and `rationale` for not-applicable), and `tools` (one entry per tool above, each with `id`, `component` when it has one, `disposition`, `evidence` and `rationale`). A follow-up finding that should be accepted as a risk carries `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; any other finding stays open. A criterion or tool you do not answer is not answered for you.\", next+1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:150:\tPreconditions   []string `json:\"preconditions,omitempty\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:390:type ReviewToolDisposition struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:411:\tTools         []ReviewToolDisposition `json:\"tools,omitempty\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:986:\t\tfor _, precondition := range tool.Preconditions {\npose-mcp/internal/pos