{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n## Decision and findings\n\nChanges requested because the ready-check’s ADR scan follows repository-controlled symlinks and reads them without a bound (N2, medium blocker). N1 is a low follow-up accepted under sealed limit L1: reviewers see the limit text in the brief and are instructed to dispute weak or broad limits.\n\n- **N1 — low, follow-up, L1:** [accepted_limits.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2742241757/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:49) counts letter runs, so `X. Y. Accepted because z w.` satisfies the format gate without a meaningful assumption or reason. This is a lexical edge of the format check; the spec assigns semantic judgment to the reviewer under L1.\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [lintspec.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2742241757/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1206) uses unbounded `os.ReadFile` for each ADR Markdown path and follows symlinks. A repository-controlled symlink can escape the project or target a non-terminating or huge source such as `/dev/zero`, hanging the ready-check or exhausting memory.\n\nR6-N1 is fixed: `reviewBundlePlanDigest` includes `accepted_limits` with `omitempty` at [review_bundle.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2742241757/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1979); the focused test passed both populated and empty-digest cases.\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| backend-observability | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence |\n| correctness | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| operability | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| requirements | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa |\n| security | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa |\n\nI verified L2 against the plan and bundle digest inputs and the empty-limit compatibility tests. The brief shows each limit as data to review, and the attestation accepts `within-limit` only for a sealed id with a nonblank reason. The plan and bundle serialize the new fields as optional; the brief version is /11 and earlier templates remain versioned. The selected design addresses the repeated-round cause by sealing assumptions and making the reviewer classify them; no structural deltas were reported. A lint-only alternative would not bind later conclusions to the reviewed limits. Revisit this choice if policy requires machine-verifiable semantic matching between finding text and limit text.\n\n## Tools\n\n| Tool | Disposition | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| artifact-check | passed (exit 0; attribution warnings noted) | command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict |\n| assess-design | passed | structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa |\n| assess-discover (pose-mcp) | passed | command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp |\n| assess-integrate | passed; three unrelated HTTP consumer gaps | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| assess-tech-debt | failed; incomplete scan and one uncovered repository marker | command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist |\n| closeout-check | deferred | review-complete precondition; no attestation permitted |\n| review-check | deferred | review-complete precondition; no attestation permitted |\n| suggest-review (pose-mcp) | passed | command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp |\n| surface-check | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration |\n| validate | passed using sealed evidence; rerun blocked by read-only Go cache/workdirs | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| validate (pose-mcp) | passed using sealed evidence; rerun blocked by read-only Go cache/workdirs | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n\nThe focused run passed: `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'`. Both strict validators completed but could not create Go build directories or cache files in the read-only sandbox. `surface-check` passed. `artifact-check` exited 0 but resolved a different active change set than the supplied sealed set; its attribution warnings were not used as subject evidence. The integration assessment’s three HTTP gaps are outside the changed paths. The tech-debt scan was incomplete on two unrelated specs; the changed Go implementation introduces no debt markers.\n\n## Rules applied\n\n- Change type: mixed feature and documentation update.\n- Workflow: `.pose/workflows/review.md`.\n- Rules: `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`.\n- Knowledge governance was not applicable because no knowledge artifact changed.\n- No handoff or contribution was written because the review boundary forbids repository edits.\n\nRecurrence check: zero flagged keys across the 14-day window. The checkout remains unchanged.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 49,\n      \"summary\": \"The lexical gate accepts placeholder-like text such as “X. Y. Accepted because z w.” because it counts letter runs, not substantive assumptions or reasons. This is a format-only residual within L1: the sealed brief exposes the limit text for the reviewer to judge and dispute.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add regression cases for placeholder-only assumptions and reasons, or make the reviewer-only semantic check explicit in the ready-check guidance.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-31\",\n      \"limit\": \"L1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\n      \"line\": 1206,\n      \"summary\": \"The ready-check reads each ADR Markdown path with unbounded os.ReadFile and follows symlinks. A repository-controlled ADR symlink can escape the project root or target a non-terminating/huge source such as /dev/zero, hanging the check or exhausting memory.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1977-1980; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' (exit 0)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept all 18 paths in the supplied bundle: limit parsing and ADR ready-check, plan/bundle sealing and both digests, draft-to-attestation mapping and within-limit blockers, review-brief/11 and immutable earlier versions, closeout finding model, manuals in both locales and scaffold copies, and the changed tests. Also checked the sealed prior finding, digest compatibility when limits are empty, input/path boundaries, and markers in changed Go files.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I checked L1 and L2 against the spec and D1/D2 against the parser, plan and bundle code. L2 is verified by digest binding and the empty-limit compatibility test. L1 leaves semantic breadth to the reviewer; the lexical weakness in N1 is disclosed as an accepted L1 follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds deterministic parsing and synchronous ADR reads, with no shared mutable state, goroutines, cancellation hooks or background lifecycle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The review plan, bundle and finding additions are optional JSON fields; the brief moved to /11 and prior templates remain versioned. Tests cover the new conclusion contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new ADR input path is unbounded and follows symlinks, allowing repository input to hang or exhaust the linter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No HTTP, event or external MCP contract was changed. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated endpoints; the scoped review path has sealed integration coverage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A non-terminating or very large ADR target can prevent any bounded diagnostic from being returned.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I checked additive fields use omitempty, the plan and bundle digest tests preserve the no-limit form, and review-brief/11 preserves earlier immutable template versions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The ready-check's word-count heuristic admits a placeholder-only assumption and reason; this is accepted only as the L1 reviewer-judgment follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The spec identifies non-converging rounds caused by unstated environmental assumptions. D1 makes limit classification an explicit reviewer judgment; D2 seals the same limits into plan and bundle digests. The structural assessment reported no deltas to map.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I compared POSE.md, the Portuguese manual, and both scaffold copies with runtime parsing, review-brief/11, and within-limit recording; the documented flow matches those behaviors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ordinary unreadable ADRs produce actionable errors, but a symlink to an unbounded source can hang the ready-check without a returned diagnostic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1-R3 are supported by the parsed/sealed brief and conclusion paths; R4's format gate accepts the placeholder-only text described in N1, an L1 follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I compared the attributed subject with the spec's plan: parser, CLI ready-check, plan/bundle/conclusion/brief code, tests, manuals and scaffold copies all serve the declared capability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The ready-check follows repository-controlled ADR symlinks and reads without a bound, crossing the project path boundary and enabling resource exhaustion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I compared lint-only handling with the selected plan/bundle/brief/conclusion flow: sealing is needed so later review uses the reviewed limits, while omitted fields preserve old records. No general threat-model DSL was added. Revisit this choice if policy requires machine-verifiable semantic matching between finding text and limit text.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0, with attribution warnings; its active index named cs-3a000dc4048f rather than the supplied cs-0e1f3afb4f75, so I did not use those warnings to judge the sealed subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97f41f9a91f96dfa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully; the assessment reported no structural deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully; it reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), none changed by this subject. Scoped review integration evidence passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs could not be read and it reported one uncovered repository marker. No TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker was introduced in the changed Go implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is review completion; this task forbids recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is review completion; this task forbids recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully: one target, 236 results, zero findings; sealed reachability evidence also passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict global rerun exited 1 before Go checks could start because the read-only sandbox denied Go work/cache creation. The sealed bundle supplies passing pose-mcp build, e2e, integration and unit evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict module rerun hit the same read-only Go work/cache failure. The sealed pose-mcp build, integration and unit refs cover the component; the focused accepted-limit/brief/conclusion tests also passed in this run.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
